<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narwar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narwar is a town in the Shivpuri district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> river, below a large hilltop fort. Associated in legend with King Nala of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, it was held by a branch of the Kachchhapaghatas and later by the Jajapellas, Tomaras, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachhwaha">Kachhwahas</a>.</p></div>
